# Library-owned overrides inheriting the House-synced root configuration.
#
# Every entry below is one that actually fires here. A rule disabled where it
# reports nothing is silent coverage loss for every file added later, not an
# exemption, so a rule this tree merely *could* justify turning off is left on.
InheritParentConfig: true

Checks: >
  -readability-magic-numbers

# readability-magic-numbers: this tree is largely a transcription of
# a wire format. The seeded report-length table, the byte-order shifts and
# masks, the report field offsets and the FRS record IDs are the specification's
# numbers, cited to the manual and section that defines each. Naming every one
# would add a layer of indirection between the code and the document it has to
# be checked against, which is the opposite of what the check is for.
